{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Meal.</b> That it not be fine flour." "<b>Barley.</b> And not wheat — she acted in the manner of an animal, and her offering is animal feed (Sotah 14)." "<b>He shall not pour oil on it.</b> That her offering not be adorned — for oil is called 'light,' and she acted in darkness." "<b>And he shall not put frankincense on it.</b> For the Matriarchs are called לְבוֹנָה, as it says ״וְאֶל גִּבְעַת הַלְּבוֹנָה״ (Song of Songs 4) — and she departed from their ways." "<b>For it is a meal-offering of jealousy.</b> This meal — קֶמַח is masculine in gender." "<b>A meal-offering of jealousy.</b> It stirs up against her two jealousies — the jealousy of the Omnipresent and the jealousy of the husband (Sifrei)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:32.146554037Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}